1058 #edb/ref 17592186544908 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544988 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "eab4f6a7-357a-59d5-b5d9-5cb4b9754a49" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544988 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186366684 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555032 #edb/ref 1080 "II only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555032 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555032 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "105104fe-d88f-5dd8-9b3a-02a1ef01ef38" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555062 #edb/ref 1080 "I only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555062 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555062 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "20c9cb4a-c332-5bc5-8dd5-fed7de433c7d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555224 #edb/ref 1080 "I and II only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555224 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555224 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "63ad22ea-66fa-50fc-bde7-f0f232d88853" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555239 #edb/ref 1080 "None of the statements are true" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555239 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555239 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "68ff13dc-9101-5cf2-bc69-4e700b97b26f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555441 #edb/ref 1080 "II and III only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555441 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555441 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "b938e797-07a9-546d-9bec-948b3e7a15fa" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555716 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186555032 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555716 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186555062 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555716 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186555224 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555716 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186555239 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555716 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186555441 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555716 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555716 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555716 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186555032 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555716 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "980312ed-2719-5060-9fbb-108e85ad677e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555850 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186555716 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555850 #edb/ref 1069 "q-100121" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555850 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555850 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the following set of polynomials:\n\n$$\n{p}_{1}(t)=t-1,\\,{p}_{2}(t)=2t+2,\\,{p}_{3}(t)=2-2t.\n$$\n\nGiven that the inner product in the vector space ${R}_{1}[t]$ of polynomials of degree at most $1$ in the variable $t$ is defined as \n\n$$\n⟨p(t),q(t)⟩=p(-1)q(-1)+p(1)q(1),\n$$\n\nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. ${p}_{1}(t)⊥̸{p}_{2}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product\n\nII. ${p}_{2}(t)⊥{p}_{3}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product\n\nIII. $S=\\{{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t),{p}_{3}(t)\\}$ is an orthogonal set with respect to the given inner product" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555850 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b4f61444-c8ba-5ff9-98c2-7150307d9838" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555850 #edb/ref 1074 "Recall that a set of vectors in an inner product space is orthogonal if all vectors in the set are mutually orthogonal with respect to the given inner product. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t)⟩ & =⟨t-1,2t+2⟩ \\\\  & =(t-1){|}_{-1}\\cdot (2t+2){|}_{-1}+(t-1){|}_{1}\\cdot (2t+2){|}_{1} \\\\  & =((-1)-1)\\cdot (2(-1)+2)+(1-1)\\cdot (2(1)+2) \\\\  & =0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich means that ${p}_{1}(t)⊥{p}_{2}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product.\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨{p}_{2}(t),{p}_{3}(t)⟩ & =⟨2t+2,2-2t⟩ \\\\  & =(2t+2){|}_{-1}\\cdot (2-2t){|}_{-1}+(2t+2){|}_{1}\\cdot (2-2t){|}_{1} \\\\  & =(2(-1)+2)\\cdot (2-2(-1))+(2(1)+2)\\cdot (2-2(1)) \\\\  & =0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich means that ${p}_{2}(t)⊥{p}_{3}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product.\n\n- Statement III is false. Let's check if ${p}_{1}(t)⊥{p}_{3}(t).$ Computing the inner product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{3}(t)⟩ & =⟨t-1,2-2t⟩ \\\\  & =(t-1){|}_{-1}\\cdot (2-2t){|}_{-1}+(t-1){|}_{1}\\cdot (2-2t){|}_{1} \\\\  & =((-1)-1)\\cdot (2-2(-1))+(1-1)\\cdot (2-2(1)) \\\\  & =-8\\ne 0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich means that ${p}_{1}(t)⊥̸{p}_{3}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product. So, the set $S$ is *not* an orthogonal set.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186558997 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186559893 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186558997 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186559903 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186558997 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186559910 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186558997 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186559935 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186558997 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186559943 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186558997 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186559980 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186558997 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186559984 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186558997 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045460 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186558997 #edb/ref 1045 "Quiz 2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186558997 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186559893 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186558997 #edb/ref 1048 #edb/ref 17592186046669 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186558997 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "17dbb386-44d9-5210-bf60-77858d50ba0a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559000 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186559892 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559000 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186559906 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559000 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186559926 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559000 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186559951 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559000 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186559976 #edb